Welcome to the team! Here is a quick overview of how the API works:

1. The app starts in create_app which sets up Flask, registers all
   route blueprints, and calls setup_logging and setup_error_handlers.

2. Authentication flow:
   - Users call register to create an account (uses hash_password)
   - Users call login to get a JWT token (uses verify_password
     and generate_jwt_token)
   - All protected routes use the require_auth decorator

3. Data access:
   - database.py has all CRUD functions: create_user, get_user,
     update_user, get_all_posts, create_post, etc.
   - models.py defines User, Post, and Comment dataclasses with
     to_dict methods for serialization

4. Route structure:
   - auth_routes.py: register, login, get_current_user, refresh_token
   - user_routes.py: list_users, get_user, update_user, delete_user
   - post_routes.py: list_posts, create_post, get_post, update_post

Start by reading create_app in app.py, then follow the login flow.
